  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "0/xxQ7LvwFk4TahnlAoHmfTiB7c=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:16.957Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Xebia scores best in the workbook on technical affinity and has real community reach through Xebia Academy and its conference presence. On the axis most leads fail \u2014 whether the bench would recognise a modern stack as its own kind of work \u2014 it scores highest of the set.\n\nTwo things hold it back, and both are about shape rather than skill. Its Dutch headcount has still not been isolated from a 7,511-person global group that is roughly 61% India-based, so what would actually be engaged is unclear; and the group as a whole is far too big for a first design partner. Community reach cuts both ways as well: a firm with an academy and a conference programme is a strong amplifier once there is something to amplify, and a poor venue for shaping something that does not exist yet.\n\nThe sequencing conclusion matches the other large agnostic firms in the set: valuable later, wrong first. Priority 3.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Xebia (NL \u00b7 7,511 global (~61% India))\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Best technical affinity in the workbook and real community reach, but NL headcount still not isolated and the group is far too big for a first partner.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:16.957297Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:16.957302Z"
    }
  },
